WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.517
Our capstone has ten design requirements.

2
00:00:02.637 --> 00:00:06.179
Eight have adequate design evidence; two
remain open.

3
00:00:06.299 --> 00:00:08.773
The arithmetic coverage is 80%,

4
00:00:08.893 --> 00:00:12.179
but there is no eighty-percent DQ
acceptance threshold.

5
00:00:12.299 --> 00:00:15.925
The first gap concerns an unspecified
contact gasket.

6
00:00:16.045 --> 00:00:20.419
The second concerns an unproven response
to a shared sensor failure.

7
00:00:20.539 --> 00:00:24.485
The diagram deliberately puts the coverage
bar beside the gaps.

8
00:00:24.605 --> 00:00:26.760
A high completion percentage does

9
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.527
not remove the importance of what is
missing.

10
00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:33.134
The supported conclusion is that this
package does

11
00:00:33.254 --> 00:00:36.688
not justify routine use or a complete
favourable

12
00:00:36.808 --> 00:00:39.390
design conclusion for the affected scope.

13
00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.240
Some limited work may continue only
through

14
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.731
the applicable documented assessment and
authorization.

15
00:00:45.851 --> 00:00:49.792
Ask what activity is proposed and whether
the gaps could affect it.

16
00:00:49.912 --> 00:00:53.454
Do not approve a blank category called
conditional release.

17
00:00:53.574 --> 00:00:57.670
Name the activity, restrictions,
responsible decision-maker

18
00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.222
and conditions that must be met first.

19
00:01:00.842 --> 00:01:04.618
Prepare a handover containing the accepted
design baseline,

20
00:01:04.738 --> 00:01:08.044
reviewed requirements, risk/control
rationale,

21
00:01:08.164 --> 00:01:11.514
open-action register and planned
verification links.

22
00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:15.282
Installation qualification will need the
correct drawings,

23
00:01:15.402 --> 00:01:18.282
specifications and component identities.

24
00:01:18.402 --> 00:01:20.535
Unresolved design choices should

25
00:01:20.655 --> 00:01:23.002
not disappear into a signature page.

26
00:01:23.122 --> 00:01:27.687
Identify which installation activities
depend on closing each gap.

27
00:01:27.807 --> 00:01:31.028
This creates a practical connection to
Module 4

28
00:01:31.148 --> 00:01:34.325
rather than implying that the next stage
starts simply

29
00:01:34.445 --> 00:01:36.445
because this course has ended.

30
00:01:37.065 --> 00:01:40.286
Your final task is to write a short
decision memo.

31
00:01:40.406 --> 00:01:43.465
State what was reviewed, what the evidence
supports,

32
00:01:43.585 --> 00:01:47.361
which important questions remain and what
action is required.

33
00:01:47.481 --> 00:01:51.790
Explain why the completion percentage does
not determine suitability.

34
00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:54.322
Compare your memo with the worked answer,

35
00:01:54.442 --> 00:01:57.148
then take the separate application
assessment.

36
00:01:57.268 --> 00:02:00.191
Course completion is self-study evidence
only.

37
00:02:00.311 --> 00:02:02.913
It does not replace supervised experience,

38
00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:08.345
an independent technical review or
authorization to perform regulated work.
